# ============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — Application Repository
# Location: place this file at .github/CODEOWNERS  (also valid: repo root
# or docs/ — .github/ is the convention for enterprise repos)
#
# HOW IT WORKS
# - When a PR touches a file, GitHub automatically requests review from the
#   owners matched below and (with branch protection enabled) BLOCKS merge
#   until each required owner group approves.
# - ORDER MATTERS: the LAST matching pattern wins. Put broad rules first,
#   specific overrides last.
# - Team handles use the form @org/team-name. Replace "org" with your
#   GitHub organization slug. Every team must have WRITE access to the repo
#   or the rule is silently ignored.
#
# REQUIRED BRANCH PROTECTION (Settings → Branches → main):
#   [x] Require a pull request before merging
#   [x] Require review from Code Owners
#   [x] Dismiss stale approvals when new commits are pushed
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEFAULT / CATCH-ALL
# Any file not matched by a later rule requires Developer review. This
# guarantees NOTHING merges without at least one accountable owner.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOURCE CODE — owned by Developers
# Explicit rules for source directories, even though the catch-all already
# covers them: being explicit survives future rule reordering and documents
# intent for auditors.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/                               @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
/app/                               @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
/lib/                               @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
/public/                            @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team

# Dependency manifests: developer-owned, since dependency changes alter the
# application supply chain. (Consider adding @org/security-team here in a
# stricter DevSecOps posture.)
package.json                        @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
package-lock.json                   @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
composer.json                       @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
composer.lock                       @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
requirements.txt                    @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
go.mod                              @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team
go.sum                              @nativedevsecops-org/dev-team

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TESTS — owned by QA
# Any change to test code, fixtures, or end-to-end suites needs QA approval,
# preventing developers from weakening or deleting tests to force a merge.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tests/                             @org/qa-team
/test/                              @org/qa-team
/e2e/                               @org/qa-team
/cypress/                           @org/qa-team
/__tests__/                         @org/qa-team

# Match test files that live NEXT TO source code rather than in a test dir.
# ** matches across directory boundaries.
**/*.test.js                        @org/qa-team
**/*.spec.js                        @org/qa-team
**/*.test.ts                        @org/qa-team
**/*.spec.ts                        @org/qa-team
**/*_test.go                        @org/qa-team
**/test_*.py                        @org/qa-team

# QA tool configuration — changing these can silently disable test runs
jest.config.js                      @org/qa-team
cypress.config.js                   @org/qa-team
playwright.config.ts                @org/qa-team
phpunit.xml                         @org/qa-team

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI/CD & AUTOMATION — owned by DevOps
# Workflows execute with repository credentials and can exfiltrate secrets
# or deploy to production; they are the highest-risk files in the repo.
# This rule is LAST among directory rules so it wins over the catch-all.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/                 @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team

# Composite actions and reusable workflow building blocks
/.github/actions/                   @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team

# Dependabot / renovate config controls automated dependency PRs
/.github/dependabot.yml             @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team

# Container build files change what ships to production
Dockerfile                          @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team
docker-compose.yml                  @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team
docker-compose.*.yml                @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team
/.dockerignore                      @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHARED OWNERSHIP — multiple teams required on one line means the PR needs
# approval from BOTH teams (one approving member from each).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This governance file itself: DevOps + Developers must both agree to change
# who owns what. Protects against a single team rewriting the rules.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @nativedevsecops-org/devops-team
